 r←IsPublicAsset path;folder
⍝ Returns 1 when `path` - what follows "Assets/" in a request - may be served, and 0 otherwise.
⍝ "Assets/Runtime/" holds what the server itself runs on: Plodder, Rumba and the certificates
⍝ together with their private keys. None of that is for anybody else, so it is never served.
⍝ The folder name is compared regardless of case and of trailing dots and blanks: Windows
⍝ opens "runtime." as readily as "Runtime".
 r←0
 :If IsSafeRelativePath path
     folder←path↑⍨¯1+path⍳'/'
     folder←(-+/∧\⌽folder∊'. ')↓folder
     r←'runtime'≢⎕C folder
 :EndIf
